Package: admng-watchdog
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: AD_MNG contributors <admng-watchdog@contoso.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: aspnetcore-runtime-10.0 (>= 10.0.13), admng-openwec (>= 0.3.0+git20260908), libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libkrb5-3, libgssapi-krb5-2, libsasl2-modules-gssapi-mit, libldap-2.5-0 | libldap2, smbclient, openssl, systemd (>= 252)
Recommends: chrony, krb5-user, nftables, libtss2-esys-3.0.2-0 | libtss2-esys-3.0.2-0t64, libtss2-mu0 | libtss2-mu-4.0.1-0t64, libtss2-rc0 | libtss2-rc0t64, libtss2-tcti-device0 | libtss2-tcti-device0t64
Conflicts: gss-ntlmssp
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: AdMng Watchdog - Active Directory change monitor
 Monitors an Active Directory domain for changes of privileged objects,
 attributes and group memberships and notifies the administrators by e-mail,
 Microsoft Teams or webhook. The HTTPS + Kerberos API is used by AD Manager.
 .
 Runs as the systemd unit admng-watchdog.service under the system user
 admng-watchdog; its history is kept in /var/lib/admng-watchdog.
